From 044a76dfd3cc8ea9cf4c3ce249ad4d22dcd06d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: the sound behind a USB-C adapter or hub as a setting,
 where the kernel names it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kernel parameter i915.pcon_hd_audio (linux-9891) gives the sound
driver PCM in 8 channels, Dolby Digital, Dolby Digital Plus and Dolby
TrueHD for a display behind a DisplayPort to HDMI converter whose
display data declare stereo only: some USB-C hubs and adapters do, while
the TV or the sound bar behind them takes more. i915 is built into the
kernel, so the parameter was to be put on the kernel line by hand.

It is now the third kernel option of the boot menus that Kodi offers
(BootOption.h): "Surround sound through this USB-C adapter or hub"
(audiooutput.hadespconaudio), in System > Audio, at the expert level,
off by default. It is shown only where the connector of the output
names it in HADES_BOOT_OPTION, which the kernel does on a DisplayPort
connector only while a converter is behind the port (linux-9892); a
DisplayPort monitor never shows it. Turning it on or off writes the
boot menus (internal-disks) and asks whether to restart, as the other
two do. Its help says in plain words that it declares formats that the
adapter does not, when to use it, and what happens if the chain does
not take them (a film without sound).

- BootOptions::Read() reads HADES_BOOT_OPTION from the kernel now, not
  the value kept from the start: on a DisplayPort connector it follows
  each detect.
- Core strings 42160 and 42161, translated in Estuary (32978 and 32979:
  es_es, es_ar, es_mx), mapped where the dialog and the messages take
  them.
- The parameter of xe (xe.pcon_hd_audio) has no setting: xe is a
  module, not built in, and kodi.log says that the connector names an
  option that this Kodi has no setting for.

The host test of BootOption.h (from 1.0) has the
third option and the tree's names and ids, and fails on the tree
before; every file changed and those that include a changed header
compiled with their commands of the build.

After the finding of PR #29 of LibreELEC Hades by Felix Oghină.
